EXTENSION "ARMDef_Through_the_Aegis_Longmist_VisSources" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Through the Aegis - Chapter Five: The Covenant of Longmist vis sources"
    VERSION "0.5.1"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_Through_the_Aegis_Core_Ext"

    # The chapter's vis sources, structured; each DESCRIPTION the source's text, verbatim.

    #t212217cbfa41022f9ecb59 ^"Tribute from the Underworld" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tOyKnFGWkxgPeCHccUaG06R3 ^"Vis Source"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Art" STRING "Corpus"
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 128
        }
        DESCRIPTION "*Four pawns of Corpus per Year* The Túatha Dé Danann entered into a pact with the covenant of Longmist many years ago. As part of that pact, while good relations persist between the Túatha Dé Danann and Longmist, they promised to lead the covenant to vis that only the Túatha Dé Danann could see.\n\nThe covenant could not have foreseen that this meant unearthing bodies from their graves.\n\nThe Túatha Dé Danann lead the covenant to a single human body each season. When unearthed, this body is found to contain one pawn of vis.\n\nThe secret, unknown to Longmist, is that the bodies themselves do not generate the vis, nor are they subject to the affects of a Magical aura or chance event; it is placed there through Túatha Dé Danann magic. The Túatha Dé Danann have their own sources of vis, but why would they go through this charade? It may be that the aim was to make the magi of Longmist party to something clandestine and unseemly, and so closer bind them in something secret.\n\n20 Build Points"
    }

    #t9a1dbfcec5b6e089668e90 ^"From the Very Walls Themselves" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tOyKnFGWkxgPeCHccUaG06R3 ^"Vis Source"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Art" STRING "Vim"
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 129
        }
        DESCRIPTION "*Four pawns Vim vis per Year* Centuries within the strong aura have taken their toll on the lesser tower of Longmist and parts of it now express vis each year. One pawn of Vim vis may be collected each season, but the vis accretes in the roof tiles, in the cobbles outside, or even in the walls. Over the years, this has resulted in the tower, the courtyard, and the roof becoming pockmarked through stones having been taken away for the vis that they contain. Some gaps have been hastily patched with mortar or stones picked from the ground.\n\nThis is, however, a Dwindling Resource, as described earlier. That means it is losing 10% of its yield each year. In effect, after three years, the yield drops to three pawns; after five years it drops to two; to one pawn after eight years; and it finally dries up altogether after ten.\n\n20 Build Points"
    }

    #t0f814c63b025d69c350f28 ^"The Swine in the Woods" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tOyKnFGWkxgPeCHccUaG06R3 ^"Vis Source"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Art" STRING "Herbam"
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 129
        }
        DESCRIPTION "*Four pawns of Herbam each Autumn* In addition to the herd of cattle and a few goats, the covenant keeps swine. They were originally brought to the covenant when a source of vis was found in the woodlands not far from Longmist. The pigs were particularly sensitive to the vis that grew in the form of mushrooms and other fungi. A trained swineherd can use the pigs to forage for the vis and take the vis-bearing morsels before the pigs eat them.\n\n20 Build Points"
    }

    #te86169e5b328ee0d08cfd9 ^"Gold Teeth from the Pike Pulled" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tOyKnFGWkxgPeCHccUaG06R3 ^"Vis Source"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Art" STRING "Terram"
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 129
        }
        DESCRIPTION "*Three Pawns of Terram per Year * There is a fearsome pike that returns to the same stretch of water each spring to take a new wife from the gathered pike. A quick and brave fisherman can catch this pike with his bare hands, wrestle it to the bank, and there extract three gleaming teeth of gold. Each of these small but sharp teeth contains a whole pawn of Terram vis.\n\nIn years gone by the covenant would hold a small feast in honor of the pike and would make its pursuit something of a competition among the covenant’s men-folk. That no longer happens and the contest with the pike is now a dangerous chore.\n\n15 Build Points"
    }

    #tc417a1720269536773ccb5 ^"The Leeward Side" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tOyKnFGWkxgPeCHccUaG06R3 ^"Vis Source"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Art" STRING "Vim"
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 129
        }
        DESCRIPTION "*8 Pawns of Vim per Year* There are certain trees in woodlands not far from Longmist where the lichen grows not on the sunward side of the trunks, but on the reverse. This lichen may be collected for two pawns of Vim vis each season.\n\n40 Build Points"
    }

    #t4285297304cb1aa019bd2f ^"The Gifted Blacksmith" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tOyKnFGWkxgPeCHccUaG06R3 ^"Vis Source"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Art" STRING "Creo"
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 129
        }
        DESCRIPTION "*2 Pawns of Creo per year* Cathal Gobha is far from Gifted, but with his forge always within a Magical aura, his work often used as the basis for enchanted items, and the raw creative forces of fire, fuel, and iron, it is not surprising that vis accumulates there.\n\nSome seasons, he finds a piece of worked iron of extreme purity that gives off its own internal heat. These glassy-black shards are too hot to be held in the hand and must be kept in water, submerged in oil, or buried in the ground in case they damage their surroundings.\n\n**Shard of Iron**\n\nCrIg 14 Pen +0, constant effect R: Personal, D: Sun, T: Ind As per the Heat of the Searing Forge spell in **ArM5**, page 140.\n\n(Effect: Base 4, +2 Sun; Modifications: +1 for 2/day, +3 triggered at sunrise/set)\n\n12 Build Points"
    }

    #t1060b914bb94949db2a3ff ^"The Needfire" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tOyKnFGWkxgPeCHccUaG06R3 ^"Vis Source"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Art" STRING "Creo"
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 130
        }
        DESCRIPTION "*Six pawns of Creo each year* In a ritual described in the Lebor Feasa Runda, on the night of Beltane, the covenant convenes on land outside the Aegis and lights a large fire built from staves of willow, hazel, alder, birch, rowan, yew, elm, oak, and ash. An individual passed three times through the smoke of the needfire benefits from an effect similar to Cheating The Reaper with a Penetration of +10, **ArM5**, page 129. This applies to any living being, whether human, animal, Fir Bolg, or otherwise.\n\nThis is pre-Hermetic magic and once the manner of making the needfire is known, it can be lit year after year, but only within a Magical aura, and the Aegis of the Hearth suppresses the effect. Where the restorative effects of the needfire are not called upon, the charred remains of the staves contain Creo vis.\n\nSome claim to have experienced visions when looking into the smoke, which suggests that the needfire may have other, as yet undiscovered, properties.\n\n30 Build Points"
    }

    #t40650dc5b7bf02d0afbdbc ^"The Black Root" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tOyKnFGWkxgPeCHccUaG06R3 ^"Vis Source"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Art" STRING "Perdo"
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 130
        }
        DESCRIPTION "*One pawn of Perdo per year* Úna, the covenant’s herbwife, has to tend her gardens well as there is a persistent presence that means harm to her herbs. Each autumn, one of her plants develops a black root. If left to grow, the root poisons all those plants around it. Once taken from the ground, the root’s power is destroyed, but it retains a pawn of Perdo vis.\n\nThe root itself may grow on any of Úna’s plants; an onion one year and a parsley plant the next. On rare occasions an additional black root may be found, either in Autumn or at some other time of the year, meaning that Úna needs to be vigilant.\n\n5 Build Points"
    }

    #t8a4408ded986c88a66759c ^"The Floating Stones of Maghera" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tOyKnFGWkxgPeCHccUaG06R3 ^"Vis Source"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Art" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 130
        }
        DESCRIPTION "*One pawn of Rego each Year* Each year, the ground in a small grove five miles north of the Maghera Falls provides one pawn of Rego vis in the form of a single stone, little bigger than a fist, that can be identified by a long stony root that protrudes from its base and secures it deep in the ground. The stone may be quite easily broken from this slender root, but at this point it takes a group of men with a combined strength of +5 to move it.\n\nEach pawn has a constant power, described below, that makes them useful as enchanted items in their own right; when moved, they remain where they are put, even if they have no natural means of support. Many of these stones have been used through the years to create floating lecterns and work tables, and to suspend large lanterns in the air among other things. These pawns, used as enchanted devices, are bought with the points for Vis Stocks, as listed above.\n\nThe source of these stones falls outside of lands recognized by the Tribunal and is therefore not protected by Hibernia’s peripheral code.\n\nReTe 14 Pen +0, constant effect R: Personal, D: Sun, T: Ind Each stone has a power similar to the Unseen Porter spell in **ArM5**, page 154, that affects the stone itself. The stones are seemingly not impeded by objects placed above it, and they have the power to hold things aloft. It takes a strong man to move one of the stones but once moved it remains where it was put, without any visible means of support.\n\n(Effect: Base 3, +2 Sun, +1 Stone; Modifications: +1 for 2/day, +3 triggered at sunrise/set)\n\n6 Build Points"
    }

    #t712f45f1c029b55b2acd78 ^"The Hunt" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tOyKnFGWkxgPeCHccUaG06R3 ^"Vis Source"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Art" STRING "Animal, Herbam"
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 130
        }
        DESCRIPTION "*Six pawns of various Arts each Year* The hills and valleys in the west of Ulaid are rich in vis that grows in the many low-level Magical auras common to this area. The pawns are found by a magus taking a ten-day distraction, though this may be spread across the four seasons. The vis is rarely the same each year, and thus requires a distraction from study to search for it. Animal and Herbam are most common.\n\nThe hunt is now rarely conducted. It is also conducted outside lands recognized by the Tribunal and so is not protected under Hibernia’s peripheral code.\n\n30 Build Points"
    }

}
